// What Dana's return has that `us` does not count on its own: the interest on the
// student loan. It counts into a line `us` reads (`adjustments`), so no copy of `us`
// is needed and no file name matters: `us` runs after the laws that count into
// what it reads.
//
// Simplified on purpose: the deduction phases out between 80,000 and 95,000 USD of
// income for a single filer; Dana's income is below it, so it is not modelled.

/// Interest paid on a student loan is deductible up to 2,500 USD a year (IRC
/// §221). It comes off income before AGI, as an adjustment.
///
/// To fix: the interest must be paid to a place of kind `student-loan-interest`;
/// `axiom why student-interest` lists what was counted.
law student-interest-deduction
  each year closing 04-15
  count min(tally(student-interest), student-loan-interest-limit[year]) as adjustments

/// Interest on a student loan, counted when it is paid.
///
/// To fix: pay the interest leg of the loan payment to an expense place of kind
/// `student-loan-interest`, and the principal leg to the loan.
law count-student-interest
  on in
  when to is student-loan-interest
  count amount as student-interest

// The most a year's student loan interest can take off income (IRC §221(b)).
param student-loan-interest-limit
  2025 2_500 USD
  2026 2_500 USD
